  "id": "COMPOUND:3429 - PROTEIN:3092",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, indirect relationship between 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid and Valacyclovir hydrolase, mediated through multiple intermediate targets. The core mechanism appears to involve the UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B17, which is targeted by both 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid and Longistyline C, ultimately leading to the activation of Valacyclovir hydrolase. This pathway highlights a potential role for 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid in modulating the activity of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B17, which in turn influences Valacyclovir hydrolase. The presence of multiple distinct targets for UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B17 suggests that the enzyme may be involved in a broader metabolic network, possibly linked to drug metabolism or detoxification processes. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B17 as a central node in the interaction between 3-hydroxyanthranilic acid and Valacyclovir hydrolase, though the exact functional significance of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
